The public community ledger makes the difference between a hope and an outcome inspectable. Its dated snapshot from the ninth of November, twenty twenty-six, lists four applications marked applied and seven prepared entries awaiting human action. It records no grant award. Applications listed there are not grants already won, and asks are not treasury balances or promises of payment. This presentation also proposes recording answers, objections, splits, awards and results openly as the process matures. Today the DAO remains offchain: no new treasury, token sale, asset migration, or member registry is created here. Artist tips are separate direct gifts from a fan's wallet, not deposits into a shared DAO pool. Read the live ledger for the latest state rather than treating this dated narration as a permanent financial record.
